    "THERMAL_THROTTLE: thermal status reached 3 during the soak, so these are numbers for a throttled device. They are real numbers; they are not a thermally-unconstrained ceiling.",
    "BATTERY_PINNED: the battery stayed at 100% for the whole soak, so it was on charge. Battery drain was not measured and must not be read off this run.",
    "NOT_DISCHARGING: the fuel gauge did not fall over the soak (+0 uAh), so the battery was not supplying the phone. battery_drain_ma is not a drain and must not be read as one.",
    "SYSTEM_POWER_IS_NOT_APP_POWER: system_power_mw is the current drawn in at the USB port times its voltage. That is the whole phone -- screen, radios and everything else -- not this process, and it is valid as a power figure only while the battery is full and taking no charging current. Read it as the difference between two soaks measured minutes apart under identical conditions, never as an absolute cost of scanning.",
